  <string name="hdr_string">HDR Scale:</string>
  <string name="brightness_string">Brightness:</string>
  <string name="hdr_tooltip">Intensity of lighting effects such as realistically bright skies and dynamic exposure. 1.0 is the default, 0 is off, values between 0 and 1 are mixing Ambient with HDR.</string>
  <!-- [EnvIntensity] Light Intensity note texts, selected in updateGammaLabel(). -->
  <string name="env_intensity_classic_note">Classic sky: Light Intensity sliders are inactive</string>
  <string name="env_intensity_classic_tooltip">This is a classic (pre-PBR) sky: a legacy sky with "auto-adjust legacy skies" (RenderSkyAutoAdjustLegacy) turned off. Classic shading mixes sun and ambient in gamma space, where a stop-based factor cannot be applied correctly, so both Light Intensity sliders are inactive on it. Turn RenderSkyAutoAdjustLegacy on, or use a sky with Reflection Probe Ambiance above 0, to use them.</string>
  <string name="env_intensity_legacy_note">Legacy sky: Sun boost above 0 EV has no effect</string>
  <string name="env_intensity_legacy_tooltip">This sky has no Reflection Probe Ambiance (legacy / non-HDR), so it skips the tonemapper: Sun / Moon boosts above 0 EV would clip and are capped at 0 EV. Negative values still work. Set Reflection Probe Ambiance above 0 to enable boosts.</string>
